{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows","id":1469907,"title":"When do you use killing blows?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-08T05:07:42-08:00","id":1469907,"title":"When do you use killing blows?","content":"I've been playing CoD for quite a while and I just thought about this, when do you actually use a killing blow? I'm talking about human games rather then supernatural (I really doubt there is a way to instantly kill a vampire or a werewolf other than fire and silver), personally I've never seen it used since even in ambush I always rolled for damage (getting some truly hilarious fails sometimes, the best being a character who failed a 10 dice roll sneak attack, talk about angering the dice gods) but I wonder how other ST deal with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T05:31:06-08:00","id":1469909,"title":"","content":"Successful ambushes only removes Defence.<br /> Killing Blows are used when the victim isn't capable of even reacting to the attempt. Unconscious, sleeping, or otherwise rendered completely paralysed. That's why it's rare to see Killing Blows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T08:41:53-08:00","id":1469920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469909#post1469909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Successful ambushes only removes Defence.<br /> Killing Blows are used when the victim isn't capable of even reacting to the attempt. Unconscious, sleeping, or otherwise rendered completely paralysed. That's why it's rare to see Killing Blows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes but what practical instances have you used or seen while playing? I'm trying to think about something that came during my last game where one of the players managed to restrain an npc with a joint lock and said that any other pc could now apply a killing blow, the way the rules are written are not particularly clear since it specifically says that it applies to opponents who are totally defenseless which is the case both when they are restrained and when they are ambushed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-08-2021, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T10:52:28-08:00","id":1469933,"title":"","content":"Under an Ambush? Not. The very movement of the person and difficulty of approaching unnoticed makes it more complicated than it seems.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 3rd ed describes this a lot better. It doesn't simply requires the target to be unable to defend, it requires the attacker to be able to carefully do as they please without constraints, taking their time to do so.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say a joint lock is always enough, but it may be depending on the situation. There comes my personal rule of thumb: what makes more sense and more fun now? I don't like to throw dice just for the sake of it, so when the enemies are already in no condition to pose significant resistance, I let my players go for killing blows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:05:11-08:00","id":1469935,"title":"","content":"&quot;Defenseless&quot; does not mean that the victim just needs to have their Defense removed. It's a case of natural language useage unfortunately overlapping with game terminology. Someone who doesn't get to apply the Defense trait can still react and move about (if not particularly far, in case of being restrained). Otherwise you'd use Killing Blow whenever you shoot at someone since human characters don't get Defense vs firearms.<br /> Killing Blow is only used when the victim is fully incapable of moving, either because that's how tightly they're being held or because they're unconscious and cannot react to an attack. It's specifically for situations where you can take your time and line up the attack without worrying about the victim moving out of the way.<br /> <br /> It's rare because you need to fulfil two conditions: It needs to be during active combat (since outside combat you'd only say they die without tracking damage), and it needs to be against an already incapacitated opponent (which is an unlikely target since if there's still active combat you still have active opponents to worry about).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:13:11-08:00","id":1469937,"title":"","content":"The threat of a Killing Blow is more likely to be used than an actual Killing Blow. Against multiple opponents, any side of the conflict may decide to take down just one, focusing effort, and then use the threat on their lives to dissuade the others from continuing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:17:39-08:00","id":1469938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469933#post1469933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under an Ambush? Not. The very movement of the person and difficulty of approaching unnoticed makes it more complicated than it seems.<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 3rd ed describes this a lot better. It doesn't simply requires the target to be unable to defend, it requires the attacker to be able to carefully do as they please without constraints, taking their time to do so.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say a joint lock is always enough, but it may be depending on the situation. There comes my personal rule of thumb: what makes more sense and more fun now? I don't like to throw dice just for the sake of it, so when the enemies are already in no condition to pose significant resistance, I let my players go for killing blows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of the ST I met ruled it the same way as you do , one in particular told me that the killing blow rule as it is, its useless and could have been just removed from the book, he preferes to simply kill the characters when its reasonable to do so. I got curious as to what other ST might approach this rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:23:22-08:00","id":1469940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469935#post1469935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Defenseless&quot; does not mean that the victim just needs to have their Defense removed. It's a case of natural language useage unfortunately overlapping with game terminology. Someone who doesn't get to apply the Defense trait can still react and move about (if not particularly far, in case of being restrained). Otherwise you'd use Killing Blow whenever you shoot at someone since human characters don't get Defense vs firearms.<br /> Killing Blow is only used when the victim is fully incapable of moving, either because that's how tightly they're being held or because they're unconscious and cannot react to an attack. It's specifically for situations where you can take your time and line up the attack without worrying about the victim moving out of the way.<br /> <br /> It's rare because you need to fulfil two conditions: It needs to be during active combat (since outside combat you'd only say they die without tracking damage), and it needs to be against an already incapacitated opponent (which is an unlikely target since if there's still active combat you still have active opponents to worry about).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why I was interested as to how other players or ST might have ruled or seen in their game how they would be applied, In combat I honestly can't see how that would work since most of the time, if the intent was to kill the ST simply ruled an npc death after an attack that filled them with lethal, out of combat, most of the ST I played with just straight up let us killed anyone that couldn't defend himself. For example in a game I was in, two armed players cornered an unarmed npc in a bathroom and instead of letting them roll, just let them kill him on the spot because realistically, there was no way the guy could have done anything about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:24:35-08:00","id":1469941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469937#post1469937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The threat of a Killing Blow is more likely to be used than an actual Killing Blow. Against multiple opponents, any side of the conflict may decide to take down just one, focusing effort, and then use the threat on their lives to dissuade the others from continuing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In that case wouldn't be a killing blow though, you would still have to roll as if in combat since they are armed and capable of defending themselves, am I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T11:28:54-08:00","id":1469942,"title":"","content":"It's for extremely niche situations. For example, if you're in combat with a werewolf and a few of their human/WB pack members on the way. If you manage to beat the werewolf unconscious but don't think you have a chance against their reinforcements after that fight, a killing blow could potentially kill the werewolf (if you can do enough damage in that attack) rather than allowing it to heal back up within a day or two. Even if you don't kill the werewolf, you'd still cause a lot more damage than a rolled attack and cause a lot of aggravated damage from wrapped around lethal, which would absolutely change how the next encounter would go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T12:05:23-08:00","id":1469944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469920#post1469920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but what practical instances have you used or seen while playing? I'm trying to think about something that came during my last game where one of the players managed to restrain an npc with a joint lock and said that any other pc could now apply a killing blow, the way the rules are written are not particularly clear since it specifically says that it applies to opponents who are totally defenseless which is the case both when they are restrained and when they are ambushed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rule its possible to do a killing blow depending on other circumstantial factors. <br /> <br /> If the players are in the middle of combat and are using this restrained character as a hostage to negotiate with other combatants I think using Killing Blow is valid if the enemy doesn't agree to the terms. <br /> <br /> If you are worried about players gaming this, make sure to toss in other enemies into combat to stop attempts at killing blows. Also it should be noted most enemies won't fight to the death and may retreat if one of their own is killed. Only to return later on with more allies and better equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T12:17:17-08:00","id":1469947,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, Killing Blow is rare to the point of unnecessary in human vs human conflict in the CofD rules.<br /> <br /> However, given as the CofD rules are both a complete set of rules for humans in the setting, and a base-line set of rules for all supernatural characters, its exists because it comes up more once supernatural conflict (humans vs. supernatural, or supernatural vs. each other) is part of play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T12:47:41-08:00","id":1469948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469941#post1469941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case wouldn't be a killing blow though, you would still have to roll as if in combat since they are armed and capable of defending themselves, am I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was incomplete. I meant that they can single out one opponent to beat them unconscious or restrain them. Then use the threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T14:38:30-08:00","id":1469959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469920#post1469920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes but what practical instances have you used or seen while playing? I'm trying to think about something that came during my last game where one of the players managed to restrain an npc with a joint lock and said that any other pc could now apply a killing blow, the way the rules are written are not particularly clear since it specifically says that it applies to opponents who are totally defenseless which is the case both when they are restrained and when they are ambushed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one time I've had killing blows come up in my game is a &quot;double tap&quot;. Basically, the hunters had taken down the monster and it was bleeding out but instead of leave it to die and not being certain that it was, they finished the job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:46:28-08:00","id":1469964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469959#post1469959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The one time I've had killing blows come up in my game is a &quot;double tap&quot;. Basically, the hunters had taken down the monster and it was bleeding out but instead of leave it to die and not being certain that it was, they finished the job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the example, I guess its more thematic than anything than, I understand why most ST don't bother with it and just straight up kill npcs when they need to, out of curiosity, what monster was that? I don't think any of the more monstrous splats (vampires, werewolves, demons etc.) can actually bleed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:49:13-08:00","id":1469966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469948#post1469948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was incomplete. I meant that they can single out one opponent to beat them unconscious or restrain them. Then use the threat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh ok, still seems gamey to me, my character in a vampire game used an npc as an hostage just by grappling and using the human shield manouver, having to beat up a single npc just to tie them ups break a bit the suspension of disbelief, still thanks for the example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T15:51:29-08:00","id":1469968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469947#post1469947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, Killing Blow is rare to the point of unnecessary in human vs human conflict in the CofD rules.<br /> <br /> However, given as the CofD rules are both a complete set of rules for humans in the setting, and a base-line set of rules for all supernatural characters, its exists because it comes up more once supernatural conflict (humans vs. supernatural, or supernatural vs. each other) is part of play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I guess it is one of those ideas that weren't developed completely, I remember in the first hunter game there was a similar merit that allowed such things to sneak attacks that made definitely more sense.<br /> Regarding the supernatural splats, I think thats where it makes more sense in some cases, like staking a vampire or if a vampire has to feed from a sleeping vessel (I think you don't need to grapple to feed if the victim is sleeping).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T16:49:29-08:00","id":1469973,"title":"","content":"Dealing with splats it may be relevant because the Killing Blow have a good chance of not end up killing the target, and this may be relevant depending on how permanent their helplessness is. Trying to off a sleeping monster will probably wake it if unsuccessful, and the creature may have ways to get rid of other bindings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T16:53:05-08:00","id":1469974,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how any of this is evidence of incomplete development. The CofD core book ephemeral entities rules don't matter to human vs. human only conflicts too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T16:59:58-08:00","id":1469977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469973#post1469973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dealing with splats it may be relevant because the Killing Blow have a good chance of not end up killing the target, and this may be relevant depending on how permanent their helplessness is. Trying to off a sleeping monster will probably wake it if unsuccessful, and the creature may have ways to get rid of other bindings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well staking a sleeping vampire (I think it takes 5 damage points to do it, which is pretty achievable with a killing blow) during the day, is probably the only safe way to deal with them other than setting them on fire, I don't know if a sleeping werewolf would be able to reflexively shift into garou after getting his health track full of lethal while aspleep (in one of my other posts, on of the authors said that they can spend essence to shift this way but I don't know if it would count if they were asleep), if you got silver though, it would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T17:03:08-08:00","id":1469978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469974#post1469974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how any of this is evidence of incomplete development. The CofD core book ephemeral entities rules don't matter to human vs. human only conflicts too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is just my impression, it doesn't look like something that was well thought out since it sounded like a solution to a non existent problem, in most games an ST wouldn't make you roll to kill an unconscious or tied up human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T17:29:50-08:00","id":1469980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469977#post1469977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well staking a sleeping vampire (I think it takes 5 damage points to do it, which is pretty achievable with a killing blow) during the day, is probably the only safe way to deal with them other than setting them on fire, I don't know if a sleeping werewolf would be able to reflexively shift into garou after getting his health track full of lethal while aspleep (in one of my other posts, on of the authors said that they can spend essence to shift this way but I don't know if it would count if they were asleep), if you got silver though, it would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule exists for all range of possibilities. You have to remember that even by the core Blue Book alone the game is still about humans dealing with supernatural stuff that breaks conventions.<br /> <br /> Someone will try to kill a supernatural creature that is tied up or unconscious, or that appears to be. Someone will do so with less than optimal tools, due to either limitations or ignorance. Someone will try to kill a vampire with a knife, for example. And there are other, stranger things in the world.<br /> <br /> What happens then? The rule exists because those creatures, known and unknown, won't be killed so easily, but won't escape unscathed either. Even if the damage isn't enough, it will have repercussions that may alter the outcome of the combat.<br /> <br /> Also, this plays out in situations like hostages, previously set or acquired in combat. What to do, then? Especially that you're focused on the PCs dealing Killing Blows, but that rule is for NPC use, too. A Killing Blow isn't just a rule to let the attacker cause lots of damage, <i>it's a rule to give the target a chance to survive</i>. You can use it to <i>save</i> characters that you want to survive in the doors of death. This kind of thing happens a lot in fiction and sometimes IRL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T17:50:54-08:00","id":1469981,"title":"","content":"It was a more &quot;generic&quot; monster, fell more under horror ruleset. They chose to double tap because they weren't sure if it had any healing abilities and weren't taking chances.<br /> <br /> As a note, demons(unchained) don't have any rules that prevent them from bleeding out. Some may have abilities to heal but not all do. They also lack an ability like a vampire's torpor that just puts them to inactivity. It is interesting that a demon doesn't have such a trait while in their demon form and not in cover though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T17:52:47-08:00","id":1469982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469974#post1469974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how any of this is evidence of incomplete development. The CofD core book ephemeral entities rules don't matter to human vs. human only conflicts too.</div> </div> </div> </div>But human vs ghost/spirit type situations do make those rules necessary in the base game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T22:32:35-08:00","id":1470008,"title":"","content":"As monteparnas noted, there are plenty of situations was you start including the supernatural where human vs. supernatural conflicts do call into question whether or not a human doing damage to a supernatural that's immobilized at the time is actually enough to kill said supernatural (or how hard it will be for said supernatural to regenerate itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T03:22:21-08:00","id":1470020,"title":"","content":"I've heard it said by a writer that fighting rules in Chronicles of Darkness are more about sneaking up on somebody in an alley and smacking them with a crowbar than choreographed action, and I think that establishes a tone for the context in which Killing Blows occur.<br /> <br /> I'd say stories that can be placed in the setting would readily include occasions where you've got somebody tied to a chair and need to make a decision about what to do with them after an interrogation. A run of the mill God-Machine cultist, for instance. You can't hold him indefinitely, and letting him go carries risks for you.<br /> <br /> I think it's not necessarily instantaneous to emphasize the brutality of such a situation.<br /> <br /> Certainly one might hope that such scenarios are uncommon within a single chronicle, but certainly should be accounted for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T04:01:07-08:00","id":1470023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1469980#post1469980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rule exists for all range of possibilities. You have to remember that even by the core Blue Book alone the game is still about humans dealing with supernatural stuff that breaks conventions.<br /> <br /> Someone will try to kill a supernatural creature that is tied up or unconscious, or that appears to be. Someone will do so with less than optimal tools, due to either limitations or ignorance. Someone will try to kill a vampire with a knife, for example. And there are other, stranger things in the world.<br /> <br /> What happens then? The rule exists because those creatures, known and unknown, won't be killed so easily, but won't escape unscathed either. Even if the damage isn't enough, it will have repercussions that may alter the outcome of the combat.<br /> <br /> Also, this plays out in situations like hostages, previously set or acquired in combat. What to do, then? Especially that you're focused on the PCs dealing Killing Blows, but that rule is for NPC use, too. A Killing Blow isn't just a rule to let the attacker cause lots of damage, <i>it's a rule to give the target a chance to survive</i>. You can use it to <i>save</i> characters that you want to survive in the doors of death. This kind of thing happens a lot in fiction and sometimes IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that it makes sense for the supernatural but not the hostage argument, lets be real here, if someone put a 9mm at your head at point blank range and pulls the trigger, you will almost certainly die, we can pull out all the freak cases we want from real life but the vast majority of people can't survive a point blank shot to the head. I understand the need to prevent a pc or npc to be executed like that but there are better ways than pretend he survived a bullet to the brain just because.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T04:05:46-08:00","id":1470024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470020#post1470020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard it said by a writer that fighting rules in Chronicles of Darkness are more about sneaking up on somebody in an alley and smacking them with a crowbar than choreographed action, and I think that establishes a tone for the context in which Killing Blows occur.<br /> <br /> I'd say stories that can be placed in the setting would readily include occasions where you've got somebody tied to a chair and need to make a decision about what to do with them after an interrogation. A run of the mill God-Machine cultist, for instance. You can't hold him indefinitely, and letting him go carries risks for you.<br /> <br /> I think it's not necessarily instantaneous to emphasize the brutality of such a situation.<br /> <br /> Certainly one might hope that such scenarios are uncommon within a single chronicle, but certainly should be accounted for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have seen such scenarios in game, basically all of the ST just killed the guy without applying the killing blow rule, I appreciate the writers intentions but I feel that the combat is not as lethal as it could be, especially when it comes to firearms, case in point, a crowbar has a bigger damage bonus than a pistol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T05:30:33-08:00","id":1470026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470024#post1470024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have seen such scenarios in game, basically all of the ST just killed the guy without applying the killing blow rule, I appreciate the writers intentions but I feel that the combat is not as lethal as it could be, especially when it comes to firearms, case in point, a crowbar has a bigger damage bonus than a pistol.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question in reality of which kinds of wounds are worse is probably beyond the scope of this discussion, but in game terms there would be the matter of how a gun can operate at range and does not generally allow Defence (penalties imposed by cover tend to cap out smaller than Defence, and cover can be shot through). In circumstances without cover and at close enough range, two or three shots that don't straight up miss will do the trick.<br /> <br /> Although it can be at least informed enough by realism in that bullet wounds can often be less immediately lethal than people would expect. People have been shot with smaller calibre bullets and not noticed until they bled severely.<br /> <br /> I'd wonder as well about their relative Initiative penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T06:10:12-08:00","id":1470027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470026#post1470026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question in reality of which kinds of wounds are worse is probably beyond the scope of this discussion, but in game terms there would be the matter of how a gun can operate at range and does not generally allow Defence (penalties imposed by cover tend to cap out smaller than Defence, and cover can be shot through). In circumstances without cover and at close enough range, two or three shots that don't straight up miss will do the trick.<br /> <br /> Although it can be at least informed enough by realism in that bullet wounds can often be less immediately lethal than people would expect. People have been shot with smaller calibre bullets and not noticed until they bled severely.<br /> <br /> I'd wonder as well about their relative Initiative penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing about real life examples is that they shouldn't be thought as common things, have people been shot by smaller caliber rounds (btw this are 25 acp, .22, .32 acp etc. not 9mm and upward) and survived? yes sure, people have also survived bigger caliber wounds, now is this going to translate into people acting like in the movies and simply shrugging off bullet wounds? not really, unless you are really lucky, even if you are hit by a bullet and survive, chances are you would still be out of the fight, there was a nice system like this in cyberpunk 2020 that had you roll everytime you were hit to simulate shock, if you failed the roll you would fall into shock and lose the round, the rolls were easy if it was just a flesh wound but they got progressively harder depending on the severity of the wound, I think that something like would make combat more realistic (for humans at least) and engaging. I know this wasn't what the thread is about but I just thought about this, sorry.<br /> <br /> Regarding the weapon initiative penalty, I actually think it makes sense for bigger weapons like baseball bat, crowbar, swords, rifles, shotguns etc. but for knives and gun it really doesn't make much sense since those are smaller and lightweight objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T07:21:07-08:00","id":1470032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470023#post1470023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that it makes sense for the supernatural but not the hostage argument, lets be real here, if someone put a 9mm at your head at point blank range and pulls the trigger, you will almost certainly die, we can pull out all the freak cases we want from real life but the vast majority of people can't survive a point blank shot to the head. I understand the need to prevent a pc or npc to be executed like that but there are better ways than pretend he survived a bullet to the brain just because.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the rule isn't just for a 9mm, but for every single instance imaginable. And it isn't for reality, it is for fiction. Those characters have a right to be freak cases if the story so demands.<br /> <br /> The freak cases, by the way, aren't so freak. The same way a disembodied head takes two minutes or more to actually die, a gunshot to the head may instantly stop a person, but they actually take time to die more often than not.<br /> <br /> Not only that, <a href=\"https://www.aans.org/en/Patients/Neurosurgical-Conditions-and-Treatments/Gunshot-Wound-Head-Trauma\" target=\"_blank\">the actual rate of survival with current medicine is of 10% of all gunshots to the head in the US alone</a>. This without considering a fictional setting where the players may have access to superior technology or magic healing for any number of reasons that can raise it significantly.<br /> <br /> Most of the time, instant deaths are a legend. Which is actually horrible, but is true. In any case, the fiction itself justifies any deviation from reality that improves the story. If you don't like this and don't want to use this, that's fine. But is not a problem with the rule, it just isn't for you.<br /> <br /> Realism is a complicated thing because it depends too much on who the reader is. <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RealityIsUnrealistic\" target=\"_blank\">When you search for actual data on common knowledge, you may come out surprised with how life actually works</a>. Or don't work. The more you learn about any subject, the more your personal perception of what's realistic changes in unexpected ways (after all, if they were expected they wouldn't have reason to change). <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AluminumChristmasTrees\" target=\"_blank\">Because of that, even creating more realistic situations may cause people to perceive something as unrealistic</a>.<br /> <br /> So chasing realism isn't a good design strategy. This is a game of fiction, not a reality simulator. And a rule may serve purposes that don't exist on your chronicle, and yet are common in another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T09:38:52-08:00","id":1470043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470032#post1470032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the rule isn't just for a 9mm, but for every single instance imaginable. And it isn't for reality, it is for fiction. Those characters have a right to be freak cases if the story so demands.<br /> <br /> The freak cases, by the way, aren't so freak. The same way a disembodied head takes two minutes or more to actually die, a gunshot to the head may instantly stop a person, but they actually take time to die more often than not.<br /> <br /> Not only that, <a href=\"https://www.aans.org/en/Patients/Neurosurgical-Conditions-and-Treatments/Gunshot-Wound-Head-Trauma\" target=\"_blank\">the actual rate of survival with current medicine is of 10% of all gunshots to the head in the US alone</a>. This without considering a fictional setting where the players may have access to superior technology or magic healing for any number of reasons that can raise it significantly.<br /> <br /> Most of the time, instant deaths are a legend. Which is actually horrible, but is true. In any case, the fiction itself justifies any deviation from reality that improves the story. If you don't like this and don't want to use this, that's fine. But is not a problem with the rule, it just isn't for you.<br /> <br /> Realism is a complicated thing because it depends too much on who the reader is. <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/RealityIsUnrealistic\" target=\"_blank\">When you search for actual data on common knowledge, you may come out surprised with how life actually works</a>. Or don't work. The more you learn about any subject, the more your personal perception of what's realistic changes in unexpected ways (after all, if they were expected they wouldn't have reason to change). <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AluminumChristmasTrees\" target=\"_blank\">Because of that, even creating more realistic situations may cause people to perceive something as unrealistic</a>.<br /> <br /> So chasing realism isn't a good design strategy. This is a game of fiction, not a reality simulator. And a rule may serve purposes that don't exist on your chronicle, and yet are common in another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with everything you said and I'm perfectly aware the instances you are talking about (I'm kinda of a gun nut in real life) but just as they are indeed within the realm of possibility, said things are also incredibly unlikely and the way the system present killing blows in relation to said instances can really stretch the suspension of disbelief.<br /> <br /> A game example, a character has another at his mercy, he decides to kill him by shooting him in the head with a pistol, he has both the intent and the will to do it but he has no dots in firearms and only one in dexterity and by adding said dot to the +1 damage bonus from the handgun, he deals a measly 2 points lethal damage, this means that to kill the other poor sod is goint to take at least 4 killing blows, which equals to shooting him 4 times in the head, now I understand that an inexperienced shooter would mess up most of his shots but to take 4 shots to the head at point blank range, to kill someone is not only ridiculous but it borders on the impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T10:10:57-08:00","id":1470046,"title":"","content":"I understand that small calibre bullets are not particularly great at getting through the skull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T10:27:55-08:00","id":1470049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470046#post1470046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that small calibre bullets are not particularly great at getting through the skull.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A .22 LR caliber bullet, one of the lowest caliber available practically everywhere, is a supersonic round and quite capable of penetrating the skull, you might not incapacitate someone on the first shot (althout its unlikely) but you are definitely going to do it on the second. The skull doesn't stop bullets, it deflects them due to its rounded shape and only when its hit at a certain and frankly unlikely angle, there are instances of .45 auto bullets getting deflected this way but they are a one in a million instances. There is also to consider that, one of the most common pistol round is the 9mm and barring freak instances like the one I wrote before, they are perfectly capable of penetrating a skull, since the manual's example of a light handgun is a glock 17 in 9mm, then it can be safely assumed that such a weapon would be perfectly capable of punching through a human skull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","user":"Newb95","date":". 12-09-2021, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T16:32:33-08:00","id":1470083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470043#post1470043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A game example, a character has another at his mercy, he decides to kill him by shooting him in the head with a pistol, he has both the intent and the will to do it but he has no dots in firearms and only one in dexterity and by adding said dot to the +1 damage bonus from the handgun, he deals a measly 2 points lethal damage, this means that to kill the other poor sod is goint to take at least 4 killing blows, which equals to shooting him 4 times in the head, now I understand that an inexperienced shooter would mess up most of his shots but to take 4 shots to the head at point blank range, to kill someone is not only ridiculous but it borders on the impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I thought this is a great example of why to use Killing Blow rather then ST fiat death.<br /> This hypothetical character probably couldn't hold the gun straight, their hand would shake uncontrollably, they probably couldn't find the safety or detach the magazine. They've never fired a gun before maybe never even held one. With the barrel of the gun pressed up against the head of their victim they're still more likely then not to hit the wall behind them.<br /> This character would be reduced to a chance die if they were to use a gun outside of a Killing Blow. <br /> <br /> That murder would be sloppy as hell, and could conceivably take four turns. <br /> <br /> Now could the ST just make it happen on the first bullet? Yes of course, but making the player have to take four turns and detailing the horrible gruesome play by play of it for the sake of drama and character development is a potent Role-play moment.<br /> It could change a players perspective from dark power fantasy to dramatic horror. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T16:43:54-08:00","id":1470085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470083#post1470083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I thought this is a great example of why to use Killing Blow rather then ST fiat death.<br /> This hypothetical character probably couldn't hold the gun straight, their hand would shake uncontrollably, they probably couldn't find the safety or detach the magazine. They've never fired a gun before maybe never even held one. With the barrel of the gun pressed up against the head of their victim they're still more likely then not to hit the wall behind them.<br /> This character would be reduced to a chance die if they were to use a gun outside of a Killing Blow.<br /> <br /> That murder would be sloppy as hell, and could conceivably take four turns.<br /> <br /> Now could the ST just make it happen on the first bullet? Yes of course, but making the player have to take four turns and detailing the horrible gruesome play by play of it for the sake of drama and character development is a potent Role-play moment.<br /> It could change a players perspective from dark power fantasy to dramatic horror.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like your view on character developement and roleplay, I really do and I wouldn't have a problem with it if we were talking about an untrained person using a knife or other melee implement since that would definitely be sloppy and gruesome but we are talking about guns here, they are the ultimate equalizer, you can take a life just by pulling a trigger and if you stick a gun at the head of a tied and maybe unconscious person and pull the trigger, 99 times out of 100 you are going to kill them, this is the simple reality of things and what I have been told by multiple storytellers (one of which was an EMT btw) when I asked them about using killing blow in similar situations. Even if the shooter is untrained, a bullet is a ridiculously lethal small piece of lead capable of doing (depending on caliber of course) a lot of damage so shooting someone 4 times, point blank in the head and not kill them borders on the impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T19:27:53-08:00","id":1470103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470085#post1470085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your view on character developement and roleplay, I really do and I wouldn't have a problem with it if we were talking about an untrained person using a knife or other melee implement since that would definitely be sloppy and gruesome but we are talking about guns here, they are the ultimate equalizer, you can take a life just by pulling a trigger and if you stick a gun at the head of a tied and maybe unconscious person and pull the trigger, 99 times out of 100 you are going to kill them, this is the simple reality of things and what I have been told by multiple storytellers (one of which was an EMT btw) when I asked them about using killing blow in similar situations. Even if the shooter is untrained, a bullet is a ridiculously lethal small piece of lead capable of doing (depending on caliber of course) a lot of damage so shooting someone 4 times, point blank in the head and not kill them borders on the impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Against a target who is a valid subject for a Killing Blow, you can almost certainly take the three turns necessary to Aim for three more dice that will translate to three more points of automatic damage. ChroD is built under the general assumption that characters will have a base dicepool of at least 4-5 in things that they're good at, and most things you're likely to be using a Killing Blow on with the assumption of a single-shot kill will have less than 10 Health, or close enough that a kick in the head will make up the difference before or after lining up the shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T00:21:51-08:00","id":1470116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470085#post1470085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">99 times out of 100 you are going to kill them, this is the simple reality of things and what I have been told by multiple storytellers (one of which was an EMT btw) when I asked them about using killing blow in similar situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The human body is an amazing combination of resilience and fragility. A lot of things will kill a human, but almost none of them will do so with any immediacy.<br /> <br /> A Killing Blow in those circumstances isn't a guaranteed kill, but it's close enough if you just apply the bleeding out rules and apply appropriate penalties for any attempts to first aid rolls to such complicated wounds. Be aware that a human can survive with the majority of their brain gone (though not without neurological issues); it's the intracranial bleeding associated with such traumas that lead to death.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dealing full lethal is pretty easy using the killing blow rules (especially combined with aiming and/or WP expenditure). If the victim is beaten unconscious, however, you only need to deal lethal damage to half their health since the previous bashing will wrap around and upgrade the remaining bashing to lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-10-2021, 03:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T06:42:13-08:00","id":1470129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470103#post1470103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Against a target who is a valid subject for a Killing Blow, you can almost certainly take the three turns necessary to Aim for three more dice that will translate to three more points of automatic damage. ChroD is built under the general assumption that characters will have a base dicepool of at least 4-5 in things that they're good at, and most things you're likely to be using a Killing Blow on with the assumption of a single-shot kill will have less than 10 Health, or close enough that a kick in the head will make up the difference before or after lining up the shot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get the system but I find it excessively gamey honestly and the fact that most of the games I had didn't bother with this mechanic, probably means that a lot of people are of the same opinion, I mean seriously? you have to thin their lifebar before killing them? what is this a videogame? I like the system and I think it has a lot of clever mechanics (social manouvering and investigations are really well thought) but I as a player, think that this mechanic was not well thought at all and it could have easily be put as &quot;If you have a human character who is, out of combat, completely unable to defend themselves, you can just kill them&quot; which is frankly what most ST do anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T06:49:45-08:00","id":1470130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470116#post1470116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The human body is an amazing combination of resilience and fragility. A lot of things will kill a human, but almost none of them will do so with any immediacy.<br /> <br /> A Killing Blow in those circumstances isn't a guaranteed kill, but it's close enough if you just apply the bleeding out rules and apply appropriate penalties for any attempts to first aid rolls to such complicated wounds. Be aware that a human can survive with the majority of their brain gone (though not without neurological issues); it's the intracranial bleeding associated with such traumas that lead to death.<br /> <br /> Edit: Dealing full lethal is pretty easy using the killing blow rules (especially combined with aiming and/or WP expenditure). If the victim is beaten unconscious, however, you only need to deal lethal damage to half their health since the previous bashing will wrap around and upgrade the remaining bashing to lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same as above, none of the games I have been in ever bothered with this things for an execution scene, they just killed the npc (and in one case the pc), I mean you want to do math and crunch numbers for shooting a tied up person in the trunk of a car? nobody would bother with such things since it kills both the realism and the flow of the game, an execution is not something that should be treated lightly in a game, I can imagine a pc character who is going to shoot the guy who killed his wife, drama oozing everywhere only for the ST to go on and say &quot;Ok tell me your attack pool and take a couple of turns to aim so that you can kill this completeley helpless asshole with your .45) I mean come on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T14:50:09-08:00","id":1470167,"title":"","content":"OK, a different approach to this:<br /> <br /> You acknowledge it's simple enough to just ignore the rule most of the time for you.<br /> <br /> Great. So what does it harm you that it's there if you and your groups will readily ignore it? If groups that do make use of it want it, and benefit to their fun for having it, and you and your group(s) aren't negatively impacted by its presence... why shouldn't it stay there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-10-2021, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T16:01:53-08:00","id":1470173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470167#post1470167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, a different approach to this:<br /> <br /> You acknowledge it's simple enough to just ignore the rule most of the time for you.<br /> <br /> Great. So what does it harm you that it's there if you and your groups will readily ignore it? If groups that do make use of it want it, and benefit to their fun for having it, and you and your group(s) aren't negatively impacted by its presence... why shouldn't it stay there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When did I say I wanted it removed? this is a forum and I was up for some brain picking and a little ranting on the side, it seems on this forum, people assume that any criticism is a declaration of hate against this or that, I just stated that I didn't didn't think this was a well thought out mechanic and that It could have been handled better, thats it, I'm not going to burn my books over it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T18:39:51-08:00","id":1470177,"title":"","content":"You've spent pretty much the whole thread saying that the rule as is shouldn't exist and should be written as something else. Splitting hairs and shifting things onto &quot;forum culture&quot; isn't really to your benefit.<br /> <br /> You've also been extremely resistant to the idea that it has value in supernatural games, for a game that assumes a supernatural setting.<br /> <br /> So yes, you yourself, in how you've conducted your posts, are responsible for the impression that you want it removed or significantly altered (in a fashion that removes the mechanics attached to it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T03:50:06-08:00","id":1470208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470177#post1470177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've spent pretty much the whole thread saying that the rule as is shouldn't exist and should be written as something else. Splitting hairs and shifting things onto &quot;forum culture&quot; isn't really to your benefit.<br /> <br /> You've also been extremely resistant to the idea that it has value in supernatural games, for a game that assumes a supernatural setting.<br /> <br /> So yes, you yourself, in how you've conducted your posts, are responsible for the impression that you want it removed or significantly altered (in a fashion that removes the mechanics attached to it).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You should read the thread again since I've said that it makes sense for supernaturals, your statement that I was &quot;extremely resistant&quot; to this is just your opinion.<br /> <br /> Please can you point to a post where I have explicitly said that the rule shouldn't exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T04:54:09-08:00","id":1470212,"title":"","content":"Going over the thread, again, to be fair? No. You've never unequivocally stated that is makes sense for supernaturals. You've always hedged it with some sort of caveat of maybe making sense for some supernaturals. You also not at all engaged with the idea that the core book has rules that might not mean much in human vs. human conflicts, but are still valid because of the nature of the setting not being human vs. human as the default.<br /> <br /> And in the post before I tried my &quot;different approach&quot; you had just argued that executions shouldn't have mechanics and should just be ST fiat. &quot; nobody would bother with such things since it kills both the realism and the flow of the game,...&quot; seems pretty clear cut that you don't think the rule should exist in its current form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T05:32:05-08:00","id":1470215,"title":"","content":"Again you are making assumptions, I have never said nor implied in any way, shape or form that the rule shouldn't exist, I just said that it could have been written differently also I really don't understand where you are getting that I am resistant to the rule for supernaturals, especially when you talk about me making caveats and such, I have esplicitly said that the rule would make sense for supernaturals and I have never implied otherwise.<br /> <br /> Regarding executions, I stand by my opinion, rolling dices and crunching numbers to kill someone that has no way at all to survive (barring some deus ex machina from the ST) is stupid and breaks the flow of the game, it would make sense if we were talking about melee weapons since those are messy and describing the messy job would be very dramatic but guns were designed to kill things quickly and efficiently and few things are as efficient as a bullet to the head.<br /> <br /> With this, I'm not saying that such a mechanic shouldn't exist simply because it would make sense if you are in combat and want to finish someone off quickly when not in a situation that can afford you the time to do it properly, so yeah you beat someone unconscious and want to finish the job before the cops or someone else comes by? by all mean use all the killing blows you need but if you are in a situation where you can take all the time in the world to do the job properly, then killing blows are pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T09:32:15-08:00","id":1470224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470215#post1470215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again you are making assumptions,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's how communication work. We think things, we try to communicate them effectively, assuming that we're being clear for the context of the statement, and then the person perceives the words, assuming that their interpretation is close enough to the intended meaning to compose a meaningful response (even potentially a statement of confusion).<br /> <br /> If you don't want to create the context where assumptions about your opinion sway towards you wanting to get rid of the Killing Blow rules... maybe don't spend most of a page talking about how you feel it's normal for STs to simply ignore it, and then rant a lot about how bad you think it is as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have never said nor implied in any way, shape or form that the rule shouldn't exist, I just said that it could have been written differently... </div> </div> </div>Again, you're splitting hairs here. Your only suggestions for it being different so far is, &quot;leave it up to the ST,&quot; or &quot;make it come up even less, with more ST fiat of death.&quot; That's implying it, as I actually said, shouldn't exist as written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also I really don't understand where you are getting that I am resistant to the rule for supernaturals, especially when you talk about me making caveats and such, I have esplicitly said that the rule would make sense for supernaturals and I have never implied otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Why did you say this then, &quot;Regarding the supernatural splats, I think thats where it makes more sense in some cases...&quot;<br /> <br /> I infer that as meaning you do not especially state that it makes sense for supernaturals, because you're saying it only makes sense for supernaturals some of the time. Why shouldn't I infer it that way? From my perspective, it just looks like you're now being inconsistent rather than I incorrectly read you the first time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it would make sense if we were talking about melee weapons... </div> </div> </div>That's a hell of a new caveat. Guns aren't &quot;clean&quot; and melee weapons are easily fatal against immobilized targets. Stabbing someone in the kidneys and not getting them medical attention is as good of a instakill as shooting them in the head; or any of a number of easily accessed areas to cause fatal hemorrhaging.<br /> <br /> The idea that breaking out the mechanics for shooting someone in the head is bad, but slitting their throat is good, baffles me. Sure someone that has no idea what they're doing can easily not cut/stab/etc. deeply enough to impact the right blood vessels, but someone that has no idea what they're doing could blow off an ear instead of penetrating the skull while aiming for the head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but guns were designed to kill things quickly and efficiently and few things are as efficient as a bullet to the head. </div> </div> </div>Guns were designed to take less physical aptitude and less time in training to deliver the same results as similar weapons. Guns didn't replace crossbows as weapons of war because guns are really any more efficient at killing than a crossbow, but because reloading a gun is a lot easier than recocking a crossbow with a combat draw strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> by all mean use all the killing blows you need </div> </div> </div>OK... so the rule is fine for the situations it's most likely to be used in?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T12:01:07-08:00","id":1470231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470224#post1470224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's how communication work. We think things, we try to communicate them effectively, assuming that we're being clear for the context of the statement, and then the person perceives the words, assuming that their interpretation is close enough to the intended meaning to compose a meaningful response (even potentially a statement of confusion).<br /> <br /> If you don't want to create the context where assumptions about your opinion sway towards you wanting to get rid of the Killing Blow rules... maybe don't spend most of a page talking about how you feel it's normal for STs to simply ignore it, and then rant a lot about how bad you think it is as written.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, you're splitting hairs here. Your only suggestions for it being different so far is, &quot;leave it up to the ST,&quot; or &quot;make it come up even less, with more ST fiat of death.&quot; That's implying it, as I actually said, shouldn't exist as written.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why did you say this then, &quot;Regarding the supernatural splats, I think thats where it makes more sense in some cases...&quot;<br /> <br /> I infer that as meaning you do not especially state that it makes sense for supernaturals, because you're saying it only makes sense for supernaturals some of the time. Why shouldn't I infer it that way? From my perspective, it just looks like you're now being inconsistent rather than I incorrectly read you the first time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's a hell of a new caveat. Guns aren't &quot;clean&quot; and melee weapons are easily fatal against immobilized targets. Stabbing someone in the kidneys and not getting them medical attention is as good of a instakill as shooting them in the head; or any of a number of easily accessed areas to cause fatal hemorrhaging.<br /> <br /> The idea that breaking out the mechanics for shooting someone in the head is bad, but slitting their throat is good, baffles me. Sure someone that has no idea what they're doing can easily not cut/stab/etc. deeply enough to impact the right blood vessels, but someone that has no idea what they're doing could blow off an ear instead of penetrating the skull while aiming for the head.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Guns were designed to take less physical aptitude and less time in training to deliver the same results as similar weapons. Guns didn't replace crossbows as weapons of war because guns are really any more efficient at killing than a crossbow, but because reloading a gun is a lot easier than recocking a crossbow with a combat draw strength.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OK... so the rule is fine for the situations it's most likely to be used in?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a stark difference between ranting about a rule and saying that it should be written differently and saying that such a rule should be removed altogether, again I'm asking you to find a sentence in the whole thread where I have even implied that the rule about killing blows should be removed, granted English is not my first language but I think I was pretty clear on my writing that I was talking about specificaly execution scenes and other situations where, in my experience, most ST don't apply the rule about killing blows, also you are making big leaps in assuming that &quot;leave it to the ST&quot; equals &quot;Shouldn't exist&quot; if anything it means that I think it should be modified to include situations where survival is nigh impossible, like the ones I mentioned before.<br /> <br /> Regarding the supernaturals, of course caveats are necessary since supernaturals are different between each other, taking as a baseline my &quot;punk in the trunk&quot; situation, regardless of how unlikely it is, a Vampire is going to laugh at a couple of bullets and indeed it might take you pumping an awfull lot of bullets in it to actually kill it, while a Changelling, who are to my understanding, still as frail as humans are (Its not a splat I have huge experience in but I don't remember them being that great at taking damage), would most likely die like a baseline human so it would be pointless to spend 3 turns and willpower to do enough damage to kill it, this are the kind of caveats I was talking about.<br /> <br /> Regarding firearms not being &quot;clean&quot; compared to melee weapons you are wrong, knives for instance, are very difficult to kill with even if you have someone totally at your mercy (just think about how many murders out there where the victim was stabbed 20+ times plus times before dying) and actually stabbing someone in the kidney or slitting their throat (think about the fact that, before more human means were invented, killing pigs cleanly was a very sought after skill) is a lot more difficult than shooting an immobilized target point blank in the head, barring some qualms of conscience and the shooter mastering the will to kill (which are perfectly valid arguments from a narrative standpoint don't get me wrong), wouldn't be that different from using a stapler gun, blowing an hear off, I'm sorry, but it would just happen if the shooter lost his nerve and started to panic.<br /> <br /> Your crossbow comparison just proves my point because what you described means that guns are just that more efficient at killing than a crossbow without requiring nearly as much skill to use, what you meant was probably damage (since crossbow bolt and arrows have the potential to create truly devastating wounds) but damage alone is not an indication of efficiency otherwise we would still be using flintlock pistols since ball ammo does more damage to a fleshy target compared to modern bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T12:51:11-08:00","id":1470234,"title":"","content":"This is pointless. If you want me to respond seriously, I'll be waiting for something that resembles a point instead of dissatisfaction that you're not getting the agreement you seem to want out of the other people in the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T13:08:36-08:00","id":1470236,"title":"","content":"I'm not looking for nobodys agreement and there is no point to be made, I started the thread looking for examples of killing blows, I derailed it a bit its true but you getting worked up over a different opinion, first by saying that I wanted to eliminate the rule (which I never even implied in my posts and it still baffles me that you would think so) and then accusing me of inconsistency. You think that the rule on killing blow is fine as it is, I think it could have been written differently, thats it, lets just agree to disagree and move on instead of getting worked up over a forum thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T17:45:42-08:00","id":1470317,"title":"","content":"I think the problem here is just that you're seeing this rule as having to be used consistently, and this isn't that kind of rule.<br /> <br /> Killing Blow, better explained, isn't for dealing damage to a defenseless target every time this comes into play, <b>but when counting the damage matters for the story</b>.<br /> <br /> This may come into play in two situations: when time matters and when you want to give a character a chance. Are the cops or enemy reinforcements coming? Do you need to leave soon for any reason? You have time to aim your attack, but not all the time in the world? If the ST decides the pressure of time is enough to cause uncertainty, then a Killing Blow rule let you calculate how much harm you cause in a given time frame.<br /> <br /> And for the ST that executed a PC? In my book, unless the player wanted the scene that way, this was a shitty job. Most often than not the player does not comes out happy at loosing a character without a chance, while number crunching, by suspending the ultimate answer for a time, actually rises drama and makes it feel fair, which is important with PCs.<br /> <br /> So here is my answer. When do I use Killing Blows? When I think haste may make for a sloppy job, or when I <b>want</b> to give a character a chance to be the 10% that survives a headshot. That and, of course, when the target is supernatural and the calculation naturally matters.<br /> <br /> Now, you <b>are</b> full of assumptions that I already talked about here. The rule isn't about guns, <b>and guns aren't magic</b>. You keep saying that survivors of head shots are exceedingly rare, but 10% isn't anything to dismiss so easily. Weapons of every kind are made to kill, and they are all extremely effective. Guns are easier, but they aren't less or more effective at killing. You totally can do a messy job with one, and for this you're comparing apples and oranges when you're insisting in comparing general knife attacks with head shots.<br /> <br /> Your sample character can cause 8 damage on a Killing Blow. 1 Dex + 1 Gun + 3 Aiming + 3 Willpower. Why shouldn't they do all that? <b>This is a <u>completely</u> untrained person <u>with extremely poor coordination</u></b>. The act of deciding to execute by itself demonstrates that spending Willpower is an easy call for me. And Aiming? Without taking aim they are taking all of 3 seconds to do the job. I think any untrained person trying to use a gun in 3 seconds should indeed get to fail. Or take several shots.<br /> <br /> Oh, a shot to the head isn't less lethal because the gun is in untrained hands. It's that untrained hands are more likely to not hit the head to begin with. Untrained people do this frequently even at point blank, there are suicide attempts where the recoil plus panic was enough to save a life. By the way, if someone that inapt is trying to execute someone else, they're probably in panic.<br /> <br /> People here, at least some of them, have a distinct perception of what is realistic than you. You think that making someone hostage in a fight is gamey. I think that risking your life in a fight is stupid and most will do anything they can to reduce that risk. You think guns are so powerful they shouldn't ever fail to kill in an execution, but melee weapons could. I disagree. This is life, not everything you see as unrealistic necessarily is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T07:01:21-08:00","id":1470342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470317#post1470317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem here is just that you're seeing this rule as having to be used consistently, and this isn't that kind of rule.<br /> <br /> Killing Blow, better explained, isn't for dealing damage to a defenseless target every time this comes into play, <b>but when counting the damage matters for the story</b>.<br /> <br /> This may come into play in two situations: when time matters and when you want to give a character a chance. Are the cops or enemy reinforcements coming? Do you need to leave soon for any reason? You have time to aim your attack, but not all the time in the world? If the ST decides the pressure of time is enough to cause uncertainty, then a Killing Blow rule let you calculate how much harm you cause in a given time frame.<br /> <br /> And for the ST that executed a PC? In my book, unless the player wanted the scene that way, this was a shitty job. Most often than not the player does not comes out happy at loosing a character without a chance, while number crunching, by suspending the ultimate answer for a time, actually rises drama and makes it feel fair, which is important with PCs.<br /> <br /> So here is my answer. When do I use Killing Blows? When I think haste may make for a sloppy job, or when I <b>want</b> to give a character a chance to be the 10% that survives a headshot. That and, of course, when the target is supernatural and the calculation naturally matters.<br /> <br /> Now, you <b>are</b> full of assumptions that I already talked about here. The rule isn't about guns, <b>and guns aren't magic</b>. You keep saying that survivors of head shots are exceedingly rare, but 10% isn't anything to dismiss so easily. Weapons of every kind are made to kill, and they are all extremely effective. Guns are easier, but they aren't less or more effective at killing. You totally can do a messy job with one, and for this you're comparing apples and oranges when you're insisting in comparing general knife attacks with head shots.<br /> <br /> Your sample character can cause 8 damage on a Killing Blow. 1 Dex + 1 Gun + 3 Aiming + 3 Willpower. Why shouldn't they do all that? <b>This is a <u>completely</u> untrained person <u>with extremely poor coordination</u></b>. The act of deciding to execute by itself demonstrates that spending Willpower is an easy call for me. And Aiming? Without taking aim they are taking all of 3 seconds to do the job. I think any untrained person trying to use a gun in 3 seconds should indeed get to fail. Or take several shots.<br /> <br /> Oh, a shot to the head isn't less lethal because the gun is in untrained hands. It's that untrained hands are more likely to not hit the head to begin with. Untrained people do this frequently even at point blank, there are suicide attempts where the recoil plus panic was enough to save a life. By the way, if someone that inapt is trying to execute someone else, they're probably in panic.<br /> <br /> People here, at least some of them, have a distinct perception of what is realistic than you. You think that making someone hostage in a fight is gamey. I think that risking your life in a fight is stupid and most will do anything they can to reduce that risk. You think guns are so powerful they shouldn't ever fail to kill in an execution, but melee weapons could. I disagree. This is life, not everything you see as unrealistic necessarily is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I absolutely agree about using killing blows when the time counts (I even wrote so) but I still think that, when timing is not an issue, killing blows are unnecessary, lets forget the whole gun vs knife thing, if it is an execution scene where time is not an issue and the ST doesn't plan on saving that particular npc, I as an ST and basically all the ST I played with, would just skip it and kill the npc since taking the time to do all the calculation is simply pointless, even if the person is untrained and does a messy job, is far more speedy for the ST to just narrate the death and move one.<br /> <br /> Regarding the PC being executed, she wanted to transition to a geist splat and so the ST had to kill her, so no dick move here.<br /> <br /> Regarding guns and knives, I don't want to get charts, data and whatnot to prove that they are, in fact, more easy to use and therefore more lethal then knives, so we will just have to agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T10:42:46-08:00","id":1470354,"title":"","content":"A useful phrase I once saw with regards to application of a Storytelling/Storyteller System game was a mechanic that was not realistic, but was informed by realism. The sense that it uses certain realistic possibilities to shape how things play out, even while the ultimate priority was the intended dramatic form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T13:52:45-08:00","id":1470371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470342#post1470342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if it is an execution scene where time is not an issue and the ST doesn't plan on saving that particular npc,</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're talking about using the rule in a situation rules aren't meant to be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T16:03:51-08:00","id":1470382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470371#post1470371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're talking about using the rule in a situation rules aren't meant to be used.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The book doesn't state that killing blows aren't meant for executions scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-13T17:02:54-08:00","id":1470393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469907-when-do-you-use-killing-blows?p=1470382#post1470382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book doesn't state that killing blows aren't meant for executions scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules aren't to be used in descriptive scenes with no dramatic stakes on the uncertainty. No rule, whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoD Core, page 68</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game systems provide rules <b>for situations where the outcome is uncertain, and<br /> it\u2019s exciting to roll dice</b> to see what befalls the characters and what their struggles<br /> accomplish. Players roll dice to see how well their characters succeed \u2014 or how<br /> miserably they fail \u2014 at overcoming obstacles and achieving their goals. Failure can<br /> be just as thrilling as success, and the systems that are explained here show how<br /> to make all of these possible outcomes work in a game. <b>Books and films contain<br /> moments when the audience is on the edge of their seats, waiting to see whether<br /> the protagonists will survive or die, win or lose, save the world or watch it burn. A<br /> storytelling game makes those moments happen by applying systems to key parts<br /> of the story</b>, and this chapter details how.</div> </div> </div> </div>No rule whatsoever is meant to be applied all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}